- TURN ORDER: if combat is just starting, note that initiative rolls are needed. If combat is
  already active, respect the existing turn order from the combat context.
- ATTACKS OF OPPORTUNITY: moving out of a threatened square, casting a spell in melee, or using
  a ranged weapon in melee provokes AoO unless the character has the relevant feat (e.g. Mobility,
  Combat Casting, Point-Blank Master). Account for AoOs in npc_actions when the player's action
  triggers them.
- COMBAT MANEUVERS: grapple, trip, disarm, bull rush, sunder, overrun use CMB vs CMD. Attempting
  a maneuver without the Improved feat provokes an AoO.
- CONCENTRATION: casting a spell while threatened or taking damage requires a Concentration check
  (DC 15 + spell level for casting defensively, DC 10 + damage dealt + spell level if damaged).
- FLANKING AND COVER: two allies threatening the same enemy grant flanking (+2 to hit). Cover
  provides +4 AC; improved cover +8. Partial cover +2.
- DAMAGE TYPES: note if the attack deals a specific damage type (slashing, piercing, bludgeoning,
  fire, cold, etc.) as this may interact with DR or resistances.
- FULL ATTACK vs STANDARD: if the player has multiple attacks (BAB +6 or higher, TWF, etc.),
  determine whether the action allows a full attack or only a standard action attack.
- POWER ATTACK: the player may declare Power Attack before rolling, taking -1 to all attack rolls
  to gain +2 to melee damage (+3 with a two-handed weapon), up to a maximum penalty equal to BAB.
  Must be declared before the roll. Does not apply to ranged attacks.
- TWO-WEAPON FIGHTING: without the feat, penalties are -4 main hand / -8 off-hand. With the TWF
  feat: -2 main hand / -2 off-hand. A light weapon in the off-hand reduces each penalty by 2.
  Both attacks are made in the same action economy as a full attack.
